 "lines": [
  "One of these nights lasts [42](forty-two) years.",
  "Pick one: spend a single night on Mercury, Venus, Mars or Uranus.",
  "You get a spacesuit, but you stay until sunrise.",
  "Pick one, two, three or four, and comment. Think fast.",
  "Number one, Mercury. The Sun sets and stays down about [88](eighty-eight) Earth days.",
  "With almost no air to hold the heat, it drops to [minus 180 °C](minus one hundred eighty Celsius).",
  "That's about [100](one hundred) degrees colder than dry ice.",
  "Number two, Venus. The Sun sets in the east, and night lasts about [58](fifty-eight) days.",
  "But the dark doesn't cool it. Thick air keeps it near [470 °C](four hundred seventy Celsius).",
  "Hot enough to melt [lead](led), with air pressing [90](ninety) times harder than on Earth.",
  "Number three, Mars. A day there is only about [40](forty) minutes longer than ours.",
  "Nights hit about [minus 70 °C](minus seventy Celsius). Cold, but nothing like the others.",
  "Look up: its tiny moon [Phobos](Foebus) rises in the west and races across the sky.",
  "And that bright evening star? It's Earth. A NASA rover photographed it.",
  "Number four, Uranus. There's no ground, so you'd float in its clouds.",
  "It's tipped on its side, so near its poles, a night lasts about [42](forty-two) years.",
  "Arrive at [20](twenty), and you'd be [62](sixty-two) before the Sun came back.",
  "So the winner is Mars: the shortest night, and a view of home.",
  "Every other pick ends badly. Especially number four, because..."
 ],
